r Center\nWasatch Weather Weenies\nUtah Weather Center\nUtah Ski Weather\nAtmos Cameras\nGet Involved\nAMS at the U\nUtah Weather Center\nResearch Experiences For Undergraduates\nUtah Ski Weather\nCollege Epicenter\nAlumni & Friends\nAlumni and Friends\nDistinguished Alumni\nEndowments\nThings Of Interest\nNews Archive\nRecent Presentations\nUniversity Covid Central\nSeminars\nRecent Publications and Awards\nPet Pallet\nHome\ngraduate\ncurrent page: Prospective Graduate Students\nProspective Graduate Students\nThe Department offers graduate courses and research opportunities leading to M.S.\nand Ph.D. degrees. Class sizes are small and offer easy and frequent interaction with\nthe faculty. The graduate program has been carefully designed to provide students\nwith a solid foundation in a broad spectrum of the atmospheric sciences while allowing\nstudents to specialize for their thesis research. Through these goals, the Department\nexpects our graduates to contribute during their professional careers to a diverse\nrange of issues that affect the public locally, nationally, and internationally. Nearly\nall of our graduate students are supported by research assistantships.\nPlease click on the links below for more information about our program and the University\nof Utah:\nResearch Groups\nM.S. Degree Information\nPh.D. Degree Information\nProspective Graduate Student Frequently Asked Questions\nFinancial Assistance Information\nHousing Information\nAbout the U\nProspective students can contact the Department at (801) 581-6136 or calvin.dittmore@utah.edu.\nApply\nInformation for International Students\nAtmospheric Sciences\nStewart Building\n270 S 1400 East Room E2108 ST\nSalt Lake City, UT 84112-0102\n801-581-6136\nStay in Touch\nFind Us\nContact Us\nWebmaster\nQuick Links\nCampus A to Z Index\nCampus Directory\nCampus Map\nShuttle Tracker\nCIS\nUMail\n@ The U\n\u00a9 2026 The University of Utah\nNondiscrimination & Accessibility\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy\nCredits & Attribu